<!doctype html>
<!-- The pages behind the front door are light, always (David, 2026-09-16), the
     way the front door itself is: one look for everything a stranger meets.
     `reader.css` guards its dark block with :not([data-theme="light"]), so the
     stamp is the whole of it, and there is no switch because there is nothing
     left to switch to. -->
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}" data-theme="light">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{% if missing %}{{ t("holding.page.not-found", "Not found") }} — {% endif %}targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('holding.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="holding">
{#- What a stranger sees. Not the product and not a sales page: the identity, an honest
    word about where it is, and the door for the people who already have a key. -#}
<div class="corner">
  <a class="enter" href="/account/signin">{{ t("holding.page.sign-in", "Sign in") }}</a>
</div>

<main class="middle">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
    <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
      <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span>targum</span>
  </a>
  {#- A state, not an action, and now it looks like one. As a pill it read as a button
      on a page with nothing else to press, which is a promise the page cannot keep. -#}
  {%- if missing %}
  {#- An address that is not a page (2026-09-14). It answered "Coming soon" with a 200,
      which told a reader with a mistyped link that the whole site was closed, and told a
      search engine there was a page there. -#}
  <p class="soon">{{ t("holding.page.we-can-t-find-that-page", "We can't find that page") }}</p>
  <p class="missing">{{ t("holding.page.it-may-have-moved-or-the-link", "It may have moved, or the link may be mistyped.") }} <a href="/library">{{ t("holding.page.go-to-the-library", "Go to the library") }}</a>.</p>
  {%- else %}
  <p class="soon">{{ t("holding.page.coming-soon", "Coming soon") }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
</main>

{#- The way in for anyone curious enough to look. It is an open-source project and the
    work is public, so there is no reason to be coy about how far along it is. -#}
{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}
</body>
</html>
